{
  "id": "2026-09-30-kafka-kraft",
  "title": "Kafka finally drops ZooKeeper, and share groups go production-ready",
  "topic": "테크",
  "level": 2,
  "voice": "en-US-AndrewMultilingualNeural",
  "sentences": [
    "Good morning!",
    "Here's your daily tech briefing.",
    "If you run Kafka, the big story this year is that ZooKeeper is finally gone.",
    "Kafka 4.x does away with it completely and runs on KRaft by default, which cuts down the operational overhead of keeping a separate coordination cluster alive.",
    "That's a big deal if you've ever been paged at three in the morning because ZooKeeper lost quorum.",
    "Kafka 4.2 also made share groups production-ready.",
    "Under the hood, share groups let several consumers read from the same partitions with individual acknowledgement, so you can build queue-like workloads without over-partitioning your topics just to add consumers.",
    "On the Kubernetes side, version 1.36 shipped with around seventy enhancements, mostly around security, AI workloads and API scalability.",
    "And if you run Kafka on Kubernetes, Strimzi has caught up with the 4.1 release.",
    "That's it for today.",
    "Pick one of these and try explaining it out loud in English — that's how it sticks."
  ],
  "summary_ko": [
    "Kafka 4.x가 ZooKeeper를 완전히 걷어내고 KRaft 단독으로 돈다 — 별도 조정 클러스터를 유지할 운영 부담이 사라졌다.",
    "4.2의 share groups가 정식이 됐다. 여러 컨슈머가 같은 파티션을 개별 ack로 읽어서, 컨슈머 늘리려고 파티션을 쪼갤 필요가 없다.",
    "Kubernetes 1.36은 보안·AI 워크로드·API 확장성 위주로 70여 개 개선. Strimzi도 4.1을 따라잡았다."
  ],
  "vocab": [
